          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInterface" name="Business Interface" id="id-912499b552c84bbd876b17f5e5b566d3">
            <documentation>Generic Business Interface: the default meaning of this type in the template, used when an element carries no specialisation. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Business Layer.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Business Processes" id="id-6b7ecc4906914b14bc89fd03479be99e">
          <documentation>Generic Business Process element. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Business Layer.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Business Process" id="id-590afdef83a046b183aeb12324cb864d">
            <documentation>Generic Business Process: the default meaning of this type in the template, used when an element carries no specialisation. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Business Layer.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Business Functions" id="id-b692dd61fd7041e5b5456539dc49e3b0">
          <documentation>Generic Business Function element. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Business Layer.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="Business Function" id="id-aff04681c31546ea9d5ff9abb40ad77a">
            <documentation>Generic Business Function: the default meaning of this type in the template, used when an element carries no specialisation. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Business Layer.</documentation>
