      <documentation>Architecture Repositories zone of the NAF architecture landscape: the architecture content of the enterprise. Approved content is on the main branch. Each element is modelled once, whatever the level or state that uses it.
Do not relate architecture content to the generic elements of the ArchiMate Metamodel or the NAF Metamodel; use the specialisations instead.</documentation>
    </folder>
    <documentation>Business layer elements. Reference Libraries: generic and NAF metamodel elements, Viewpoints. Architecture Repositories: the enterprise's content.</documentation>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Application" id="id-26bae2d8dddf40cb9521fda865207337" type="application">
    <folder name="Reference Libraries" id="id-3d54c9237cb34fc6a5d55de3be309117">
      <folder name="ArchiMate Metamodel" id="id-c9339e8e0f9440d7b78f406a07fd22eb">
        <folder name="Application Components" id="id-ed0fcab2c2854094b33def503b0cc44e">
          <documentation>Generic Application Component element. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Application Layer.</documentation>
