        </folder>
        <folder name="Gaps" id="id-9ed74eca386f4c94bce7b70bf9d4183e">
          <documentation>Generic Gap element. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Implementation and Migration Elements.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Gap" name="Gap" id="id-fe7affe0bec04f4eb016bf11913a64fe">
            <documentation>Generic Gap: the default meaning of this type in the template, used when an element carries no specialisation. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Implementation and Migration Elements. Not used by the NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide; available in this template (decision S1).</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <documentation>One generic element per ArchiMate 3.2 type, carrying the default meaning of the type in this template.</documentation>
      </folder>
      <folder name="NAF Metamodel" id="id-decc6a0039bf484b929c5fadc36c56e0">
        <folder name="Deliverables" id="id-8bcabd6ada994c80a1c72f3fa0d6c2e3">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Deliverable elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Deliverable" name="Architecture Work Product" id="id-00d89e4431ca4a20ab38bd8e18acfd05" profiles="id-ff2e2bdf90794a79a57d5dfe271abfcc">
            <documentation>A defined result of architecture work; its status is the Architecture Status property. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Implementation Events" id="id-7cb7060129294a29ae120deecad912f7">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Implementation Event elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ImplementationEvent" name="Architecture Milestone" id="id-1753610765704f508a778b302f08f5cd" profiles="id-cde21340481548bb94c2f34907316efa">
            <documentation>A point in time at which architecture work products reach a given status. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ImplementationEvent" name="Milestone" id="id-562916ba905244abab5d8ef0ae462d27" profiles="id-aa6d25b38e0e4b60a223c35a021538f4">
            <documentation>A significant point in the development of a capability, a logical element or a resource. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Plateaus" id="id-2053ea71d1de40beae83647a67071700">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Plateau elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Plateau" name="Enterprise Phase" id="id-c58b90a09cd946c6825b35bd565d7576" profiles="id-126f77b610724f4fb204e375ab2da22a">
            <documentation>A current or future state of the enterprise over a period of time. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Work Packages" id="id-122b725708bf40778bef4089e0e76331">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Work Package elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:WorkPackage" name="Architecture Project" id="id-8591568bc9ca4e88b342890ac69d6d40" profiles="id-91dc016d9e19479780ee6a83783496ca">
            <documentation>A project that produces architecture work products. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <documentation>One element per NAF specialisation created in this template (see the mapping table).</documentation>
      </folder>
      <folder name="Reference Architectures" id="id-b106b1a6562842a1b7f65022c0419991">
        <documentation>Reusable reference architectures. Empty in the template.</documentation>
      </folder>
      <documentation>Reference Libraries zone of the NAF architecture landscape: reusable reference content. Not modified in an instance; updated by importing a new release of the template.</documentation>
    </folder>
