            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-ad1d6def925e4dcd83a79301b63d3ae0" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="800" y="20" width="460" height="459"/>
              <content>Purpose – Set the scope of the architecture effort and give the strategic context of the capabilities.

Concerns – Enterprise strategy · Capability planning · Capturing and communicating the strategic vision of capability evolution.

Scope – Shall: the enterprise vision and the capabilities it requires; the goals it specifies; the enterprise phases in which the capabilities are desired. May: the effects the capabilities aim at; enduring tasks linked to capabilities and goals.

Modelling rules – The Enterprise Vision is a Goal specialised « Enterprise Vision » that aggregates the goals it specifies. Capabilities influence the vision and the goals they contribute to. Effects are Outcomes realised by capabilities and realising goals. Enterprise Phases (Plateau) aggregate the capabilities, goals and effects of the phase. Enduring Tasks are modelled as Capabilities.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Enterprise Vision: Goal only (not Driver); Goal: Goal only (Outcome reserved for Effect).

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / C Concepts / C2 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Sets the scope of the architecture effort and the strategic context of the capabilities: vision, goals, required capabilities and enterprise phases.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="C2"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="C – Concepts"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="2 – Structure"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AV, AD, AE, AG"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Strategy"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (C2); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 6"/>
          </element>
