            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-be4112dc33394f66a77755c268433c77" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="610" y="20" width="460" height="374"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify the dependencies between capabilities.

Concerns – Capability management · Analysing dependencies between capabilities and between capability groups.

Scope – Shall: all dependencies between the capabilities relevant to the entity of interest. May: the capability groups and the dependencies between them; capability specialisations.

Modelling rules – A dependency is a serving relationship from the capability depended on to the dependent capability; it is mandatory in this view. Capability Groups (Grouping) aggregate capabilities and other groups, and serve each other.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – None.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / C Concepts / C3 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the dependencies between capabilities and between capability groups.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="C3"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="C – Concepts"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="3 – Connectivity"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE, MP"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Capability Map"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (C3); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 7"/>
          </element>
