            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-17c49bdd9df2421eac09ee6a671aefc9" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="610" y="20" width="460" height="391"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify the processes and trace them to the capabilities they support.

Concerns – Producing doctrine · Operational analysis · Specifying doctrine.

Scope – Shall: the operational activities relevant to the entity of interest and the capabilities they support. May: standard operational activities supporting capabilities.

Modelling rules – Operational Activities and standard operational activities are Business Processes specialised « Operational Activity » that realise capabilities. Standard activities are distinguished by their name or documentation, not by another type. Decompose activities by composition.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Operational Activity: Business Process only (Value Stream not used).

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / C Concepts / C4 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the operational activities and traces them to the capabilities they support.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="C4"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="C – Concepts"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="4 – Processes"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Strategy"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (C4); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 8"/>
          </element>
