            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-0e9d8f592ad443078cc04a0aaa432bb9" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="990" y="20" width="460" height="391"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify and describe the effects the capabilities aim at, and the effectiveness criteria set for them.

Concerns – Operational analysis · Analysis of non-functional properties · Characterising the expected results.

Scope – Shall: the effects the capabilities aim at. May: the effectiveness criteria specified by capabilities or characterising effects; the measures evaluating them.

Modelling rules – Effects are Outcomes realised by capabilities. Effectiveness Criteria (Requirement) are realised by capabilities and realise outcomes. Measures (Business Object) are associated with the criteria they evaluate; a target value may instead be recorded as a property of the criteria.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – None.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / C Concepts / C5 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the effects the capabilities aim at and the effectiveness criteria set for them.</documentation>
