            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-2188cabbed184847b83620d17c6e1c60" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="990" y="20" width="460" height="391"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify and describe the categories of measures (assessment criteria) and the capabilities they apply to.

Concerns – Capability planning and management · Setting capability assessment criteria · Military estimates.

Scope – Shall: the capabilities characterised by assessment criteria; the measures evaluating these criteria. May: effectiveness criteria specified by capabilities and evaluated by measures.

Modelling rules – Assessment and Effectiveness Criteria are Requirements realised by the capabilities they apply to. Measures (Business Object) are associated with the criteria they evaluate; target values may be recorded as properties of the criteria.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – None.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / C Concepts / C7 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the categories of measures (assessment criteria) and the capabilities they apply to.</documentation>
