            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-64d1696459a445e0b1ab9518e3cd9471" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="800" y="20" width="460" height="408"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify and describe the assumptions (strategic constraints) that frame capability planning.

Concerns – Capability planning · Planning assumptions · Implementation planning.

Scope – Shall: the capabilities relevant to the entity of interest and the strategic constraints that apply to them. May: the strategic rationale of the constraints; the effects the capabilities aim at; the vision requiring the capability and the goals it specifies.

Modelling rules – Strategic Constraints are Constraints associated with the capabilities they apply to. A Rationale (Driver) influences the constraint it justifies. Effects, vision and goals follow the rules of C2.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Strategic Constraint: Constraint instead of Requirement; Enterprise Vision: Goal only; Goal: Goal only.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / C Concepts / C8 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the strategic constraints (planning assumptions) that apply to the capabilities, with their rationale.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="C8"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="C – Concepts"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="8 – Constraints"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE, MP"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Motivation"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (C8); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 11"/>
          </element>
