            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-e563208b755e4f75a9deb8d4e45f1f86" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="616" y="20" width="460" height="459"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify the capability milestones, the capability increments they mark and the capabilities these increments deliver.

Concerns – Capability planning · Acquisition management · Capability phasing.

Scope – Shall: the capability milestones; the capability increments they define; the capabilities the increments deliver. May: enterprise phases, their ordering and grouping; capability projects scheduling the milestones; capability configurations traced to capabilities.

Modelling rules – A capability is composed of its increments (Capability). A Milestone (Implementation Event) is associated with the increment it marks; projects (Work Package) realise increments and trigger milestones. Enterprise Phases (Plateau) aggregate increments and trigger or aggregate other phases. Dates go in properties or in the documentation of milestones.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Capability project: Work Package without specialisation (decision S2); project to milestone: triggering instead of association.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / C Concepts / Cr &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Shows the capability milestones, the capability increments they mark and the capabilities these increments deliver.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="Cr"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="C – Concepts"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="r – Roadmap"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AV, AD, AE, MP"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Implementation and Migration"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (Cr); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 12"/>
          </element>
        </folder>
