            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-06ea144fadb64f0f8ffe06e44f92db60" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="990" y="20" width="460" height="391"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify service specifications and organise them in specialisation taxonomies.

Concerns – Service planning · Service audit · Identification of services.

Scope – Shall: all services relevant to the entity of interest, organised in specialisation taxonomies. May: service groups and their groupings; the service policies that services satisfy.

Modelling rules – Use the three service layers (business, application, technology) wherever layering applies to the architecture. Specialisation relates services of the same layer. A Service Group (Product) aggregates services and other groups. A Service Policy (Requirement) is realised by the services that satisfy it.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – None.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / S Service Specifications / S1 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies service specifications and organises them in specialisation taxonomies.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="S1"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="S – Service Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="1 – Taxonomy"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AV, AD, AE, AG"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Product"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (S1); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 13"/>
          </element>
