            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-7502a8a1409a481aa084584e1227c80f" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="815" y="20" width="460" height="476"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify and specify the service interfaces.

Concerns – Service implementation guidance · Service interoperability · Service integration · Definition of service interfaces and their boundaries.

Scope – Shall: the interfaces specified by each service. May: the operations of the interfaces; the parameters of the operations; the physical passive resources these parameters involve.

Modelling rules – Use the three layers wherever layering applies. Each service is assigned to at least one interface. An Operation (Function) realises the service and is associated with the interface that specifies it. Parameters (Business Object) are accessed by operations and realised by physical passive resources. A data model is reached through the physical passive resource (see P7).

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Operation to Interface: association instead of serving; Operation to Service: realization added; Service Operation Parameter: Business Object only (Artifact alternative dropped, decision S5); physical passive resource to parameter: realization instead of association.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / S Service Specifications / S3 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies and specifies the interfaces of services, their operations and the parameters of these operations.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="S3"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="S – Service Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="3 – Connectivity"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Layered"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (S3); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 15"/>
          </element>
