            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-800835c4307149f2aad9ba1727eaa66d" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="616" y="20" width="460" height="476"/>
              <content>Purpose – Define the behaviour of a service through the functions and operational activities that enable it.

Concerns – Level of detail required by a service · Outline requirements for service behaviour · Service implementation guidance · Service specification and planning.

Scope – Shall: all service functions enabling the services. May: groupings of service functions; the providers and consumers of the functions or services; the operational activities supporting or enabled by the functions, and those performed by providers or consumers.

Modelling rules – Functions realise the service of their layer and aggregate functions of the same type. Providers are logical active resources assigned to the functions of their layer, or a Node (Grouping) aggregating them while their nature is unknown (see L1). Consumers are served by the service.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Service Function to Service: realization instead of serving; Node to function and activity: aggregation instead of assignment (a Grouping groups, it does not perform).

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / S Service Specifications / S4 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Defines the behaviour of services through the functions and operational activities that enable them.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="S4"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="S – Service Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="4 – Processes"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Service Realization"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (S4); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 16"/>
          </element>
