            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-ddff6f3a9e83442a8c9b43b476274c43" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="625" y="20" width="460" height="527"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify the possible states of a service and the transitions between them.

Concerns – Level of detail required by a service · Outline requirements for service behaviour · Service implementation guidance · Service behaviour specification.

Scope – Shall: all states of the service relevant to the entity of interest; the transitions between them. May: the events triggering the transitions; the service functions enabling the service and their modes.

Modelling rules – States and transitions are properties of the service, not elements (decision S11): `State` (repeated), `Initial State`, `State Transition` in the form `&lt;From> -> &lt;To> [&lt;Event>]`, where the event is the exact name of a Logical Event triggering the service. Modes are `Mode` properties of the service function; a state may be prefixed by its mode (`&lt;Mode>: &lt;State>`). Label of the service in the view: `${name}` then `States: ${properties:, :State}`.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Service State, Service State Transition and Service Mode: properties instead of events and interactions (decision S11); Service State Group: not represented; functions enabled by a state: not represented; Logical Event triggers the service, the transition being named in the property.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / S Service Specifications / S5 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the possible states of a service, the transitions between them and the events triggering these transitions.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="S5"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="S – Service Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="5 – States"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Service Realization"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (S5); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 17"/>
          </element>
