            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-77ddac9da3564ec5868fc85581eae21f" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="899" y="20" width="460" height="527"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify and specify all the parameters used by the service functions and operations in scope.

Concerns – Detailed service design · Service compatibility analysis · Service-oriented architecture governance · Service interoperability.

Scope – Shall: the parameters of the service functions and operations relevant to the entity of interest; the passive resources these parameters involve. May: the services enabled by the functions; the interfaces specifying the operations and the services specifying these interfaces.

Modelling rules – Service functions usually describe the problem space and involve logical passive resources; operations describe the technical solution and involve physical passive resources. Both styles may be combined. Parameters (Business Object) are accessed by their function or operation. The rules of S3 apply to services, interfaces and operations.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Passive resources follow the NAF information model: Service Function Parameter with logical passive resources, Service Operation Parameter with physical passive resources (the guide pairs them the other way round); physical passive resource to parameter: realization instead of association; Operation to Interface: association instead of serving.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / S Service Specifications / S7 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies and specifies the parameters of service functions and service operations, and the passive resources they involve.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="S7"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="S – Service Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="7 – Information"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Layered"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (S7); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 19"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="S8 Service Constraints" id="id-3a53ecff1f784a338c0ad2b86fa7211f">
