            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-f4b4f4d3a3d24e819b3da30fa1cc2241" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="990" y="20" width="460" height="408"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify and describe the rules and constraints applying to the implementation, operation and use of services.

Concerns – Service design · Contracting for services · User and system requirements · Service governance.

Scope – Shall: the service constraints, grouped by service policies. May: the services satisfying the policies; the measures by which the constraints are evaluated.

Modelling rules – A Service Policy (Requirement) aggregates Constraints and is realised by the services satisfying it. A Measure (Business Object) is associated with the constraints it evaluates; target values may be recorded as properties of the constraint.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Service Constraint: Constraint instead of a specialised Requirement.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / S Service Specifications / S8 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the rules and constraints applying to the implementation, operation and use of services, grouped by service policy.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="S8"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="S – Service Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="8 – Constraints"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE, MP"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Requirements Realization"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (S8); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 20"/>
          </element>
