            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-e1a20bb291e644a8932f5c2b33e0dc3b" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="643" y="20" width="460" height="459"/>
              <content>Purpose – Show the service milestones related to the evolution of services.

Concerns – Service life cycle planning · Acquisition management · Service phasing · Service gap and surplus analysis · Service-oriented architecture governance.

Scope – Shall: the service milestones defining service readiness levels; the services fulfilling these levels. May: the service projects scheduling the milestones and defining the evolution of the services.

Modelling rules – A Milestone (Implementation Event) carries the readiness level it defines in its `Readiness Level` property and is associated with the services that reach it. Projects (Work Package) realise the services they evolve and trigger the milestones they schedule. Dates go in properties or in the documentation of milestones.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Service Readiness Level: property of the milestone instead of a Plateau; service project: Work Package without specialisation (decision S2); project to milestone: triggering instead of association.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / S Service Specifications / Sr &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Shows the service milestones, the readiness levels they define and the services that reach them.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="Sr"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="S – Service Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="r – Roadmap"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AV, AD, AE, MP"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Implementation and Migration"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (Sr); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 21"/>
          </element>
