            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-9889a57bf3534d6f81afb9f29bb9c695" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="616" y="20" width="460" height="357"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify the services that enable capabilities.

Concerns – Mapping capabilities to the services that support them · Service specification and planning.

Scope – Shall: the services and capabilities relevant to the architecture, and the links from services to the capabilities they enable or contribute to.

Modelling rules – Use the three service layers wherever layering applies to the architecture. Each service realises the capabilities it enables. A matrix of this view can be produced by a jArchi report.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – None.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / S Service Specifications / C1-S1 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Maps the services to the capabilities they enable or contribute to.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="C1-S1"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="C – Concepts / S – Service Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="1 – Taxonomy"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="— (not listed in the NAF stage tables; use with C1 and S1)"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Strategy"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (C1-S1); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 22"/>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="L Logical Specifications" id="id-902c800ff1744f088ddaf36a049aebe1">
          <documentation>NAF Viewpoint Guides of grid row L Logical Specifications.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="L1 Logical Taxonomy" id="id-ba6902aa9d8a41ca810e99ad18d0bb2a">
