            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-9c36d0c1b92643bdbd8b181496b9464d" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="610" y="20" width="460" height="408"/>
              <content>Purpose – Present the logical concept of a scenario in a form readable by all stakeholders.

Concerns – Architecture context of the enterprise or project (the NAF uses this viewpoint as Architecture Context Diagram) · Definition of operational concepts.

Scope – May: a rich picture; the nodes and the needlines between them.

Modelling rules – The view may combine pictures (images in Notes or Groups) with nodes and needlines, which follow the rules of L2. Pictures are illustrations, not model content.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Needline: specialised association instead of a flow. The NAF lists no concerns for L2-L3: the concerns above are derived from its use as Architecture Context Diagram in the stage tables of NAF v4.1 ch. 2.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / L Logical Specifications / L2-L3 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Presents the logical concept of the scenario, usually as a rich picture, possibly with nodes and needlines.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="L2-L3"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="L – Logical Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="2 – Structure / 3 – Connectivity"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AV, AD, AE, AG"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="—"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (L2-L3), ch. 2 tables 2.5 to 2.7 and 2.9 (Architecture Context Diagram); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 25"/>
          </element>
