            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-a9046096d3ef4bf4add7d1d21b1b8419" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="806" y="20" width="460" height="476"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify all relevant interactions between nodes, through the logical active resources they group.

Concerns – Interoperability requirements.

Scope – Shall: the logical interactions between the logical active resources relevant to the entity of interest; the logical passive resources they convey. May: the needlines the interactions answer, with the nodes and the logical resources they aggregate; the passive resources asked for by the needlines.

Modelling rules – A logical interaction is a flow between two logical active resources of any type, named after what is exchanged; conveyed resources are associated with the flow. An Interaction element (Business Interaction) is used only for a collective behaviour of several actors or roles. The flows between the resources of two nodes answer the needline between these nodes (L2).

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Logical Interaction: flow between logical active resources by default (the guide's first option), the Interaction element being kept for actors and roles only; Needline: specialised association.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / L Logical Specifications / L3 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the interactions between logical active resources and the logical passive resources they convey.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="L3"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="L – Logical Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="3 – Connectivity"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="—"/>
