            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-9feeb6aae8c74210a690d9cf4de07c19" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="800" y="20" width="460" height="612"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify the operational activities, their grouping and composition, and the flows between them.

Concerns – Description of business processes and workflows · Operational planning · Concept of operations · Service orchestration · Requirements capture, derivation and traceability · Logistics support analysis · Information flow analysis · Support task analysis to determine training needs · Mission threads.

Scope – Shall: the operational control flows between operational activities; the nodes, or the roles they hold, performing the activities. May: logical events triggering or triggered by activities; operational flows; logical passive resources acted upon or conveyed; capabilities supported; services and physical active resources traced to the activities.

Modelling rules – Control flow is triggering; an Operational Flow is a specialised flow between activities, with conveyed resources associated with it (Logical Material and Logical Energy as Information Object). Roles are assigned to the activities they perform; a Node aggregates the roles it holds and the activities it performs; Actors may be assigned like roles. Swim lanes may be drawn with the Node groupings. Light guide: traces to services (serving, see S4) and to physical active resources (serving or assignment, see L4-P4) are allowed but not drawn.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Operational Flow: specialised flow instead of a business collaboration; Node to Role and activity: aggregation instead of assignment (a Grouping groups, it does not perform); passive resources conveyed by a flow: association to the flow instead of access from a collaboration.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / L Logical Specifications / L4 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the operational activities, their composition, the control flows and operational flows between them, and the nodes or roles performing them.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="L4"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="L – Logical Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="4 – Processes"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Business Process Cooperation"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (L4); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 27"/>
          </element>
