            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-76894277381d44d7b5a1dcd83f2e5dcc" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="625" y="20" width="460" height="527"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify the possible states or modes of a node's logical resources and the transitions between states.

Concerns – User requirements specification · Analysis of business events · Behavioural analysis.

Scope – Shall: all states of the logical active resources relevant to the entity of interest; the transitions between them. May: the events triggering the transitions; the modes of logical functions and operational activities.

Modelling rules – Convention of decision S11: `State` (repeated), `Initial State` and `State Transition` (`&lt;From> -> &lt;To> [&lt;Event>]`) are properties of the logical active resource; `Mode` is a property of the logical function or operational activity; a state may be prefixed by its mode. The event named in a transition is a Logical Event associated with the resource. Label: `${name}` then `States: ${properties:, :State}`. Use the typed logical resources (elaborated in L3); a Node may carry states while its nature is unknown.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Logical State, Logical Transition and Logical Mode: properties instead of events and interactions (decision S11); Logical State Group and functions enabled by a state: not represented; event to resource: association (an event cannot trigger an active structure element).

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / L Logical Specifications / L5 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the possible states and modes of logical active resources, the transitions between states and the events triggering them.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="L5"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="L – Logical Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="5 – States"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="—"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (L5); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 28"/>
          </element>
