            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-a67d2a86f990452aab1a33de6129cbc9" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="800" y="20" width="460" height="476"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify the information products, information entities and their relationships.

Concerns – Information requirements · Message requirements · Information models · Information architecture · Information product hierarchy.

Scope – Shall: the information entities relevant to the entity of interest. May: the information models specifying them; their attributes and attribute types; the information products the models represent.

Modelling rules – Entities, models and products are Information Objects, distinguished by their name and documentation. A model aggregates the entities it specifies; an association names a relationship between entities or links a product to the model it represents. Attributes are properties of the entity: key `Attribute` repeated, value `&lt;name>: &lt;type>`. ArchiMate is not a data modelling notation: detailed data models belong to P7 or to a dedicated tool.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Information Attribute and Information Attribute Type: properties of the entity instead of business objects.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / L Logical Specifications / L7 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the information entities, the information models specifying them, the information products they represent, and their relationships.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="L7"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="L – Logical Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="7 – Information"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Information Structure"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (L7); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 30"/>
          </element>
