            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-41fe8430113b40d2bd096efd66a78bd1" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="1161" y="20" width="460" height="459"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify and describe the logical constraints and logical requirements.

Concerns – Non-functional user requirements specification · Definition of business rules · Identification of operational constraints.

Scope – Shall: the logical requirements and the logical constraints they relate to; the logical active resources, behaviour and passive resources they apply to. May: the logical specifications grouping them; the rationale of the constraints, traced to strategic constraints.

Modelling rules – Requirements and Constraints are realised by the elements they apply to. A Logical Specification (Requirement) aggregates requirements and constraints. A Rationale (Driver) influences the constraint it justifies and is influenced by the strategic constraint it derives from (Constraint, see C8).

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Logical Constraint: Constraint instead of a specialised Requirement; Logical Specification: Requirement only (no Grouping alternative, decision S5).

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / L Logical Specifications / L8 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the logical requirements and constraints, and the logical resources and behaviour they apply to.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="L8"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="L – Logical Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="8 – Constraints"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE, MP"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Requirements Realization"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (L8); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 31"/>
          </element>
