            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-e5cd696ee48a446eaba8f570c601eb25" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="643" y="20" width="460" height="510"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify logical roadmaps, with the logical milestones related to the evolution of the logical building blocks.

Concerns – Acquisition planning · Portfolio and programme management · Project performance reporting · Project management and control, including delivery timescales · Project dependencies and associated risks · Through-life management planning.

Scope – Shall: the logical milestones defining readiness levels; the logical active resources fulfilling them. May: the capability increments the readiness levels relate to; the logical projects scheduling the milestones and defining the evolution of the resources.

Modelling rules – As Sr: a Milestone (Implementation Event) carries its `Readiness Level` property and is associated with the resources reaching it and with the capability increment it relates to (see Cr). Projects (Work Package) realise the resources they evolve and trigger the milestones they schedule.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Logical Readiness Level: property of the milestone instead of a Plateau; logical project: Work Package without specialisation (decision S2); project to milestone: triggering instead of association.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / L Logical Specifications / Lr &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Shows the logical milestones, the readiness levels they define and the logical active resources that reach them.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="Lr"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="L – Logical Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="r – Roadmap"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AV, AD, AE, MP"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Implementation and Migration"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (Lr); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 32"/>
          </element>
        </folder>
