            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-56fe7fdb80cf44d9948c02be3d65f60a" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="824" y="20" width="460" height="561"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify how physical resources are structured and how they depend on other resources, organised into capability configurations.

Concerns – Physical architecture · Systems engineering and design · Organizational design · Systems integration and its management · System requirements specification · Definition of system concepts and options · Human-system interactions · Interface requirements capture · Capability integration planning · Operational planning (capability configuration definition).

Scope – Shall: physical active and passive resources organised into capability configurations; their structure; the dependencies between active and passive resources. May: resource interactions between active resources; traces of passive resources to logical passive resources.

Modelling rules – A Capability Configuration (Grouping) aggregates the resources it combines. Composition structures resources of the same type; persons belong to organizations by aggregation. Active resources access the passive resources they depend on. A physical passive resource realises the logical passive resource it implements. Serving relations between resources are allowed and not drawn.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Resource interaction: flow between resources (as L3), detailed in P3; trace of interactions to logical interactions: through the resources (P1), not between relationships.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / P Physical Resource Specifications / P2 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies how physical resources are organised into capability configurations, how they are structured and the passive resources they depend on.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="P2"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="P – Physical Resource Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="2 – Structure"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE, AG"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Physical"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (P2); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 34"/>
          </element>
