            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-c73871d8c4fa4be38946cd87d2d412f2" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="800" y="20" width="460" height="595"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify all relevant interactions between physical active resources.

Concerns – Interface specification · Systems engineering · System requirements · Identification of interactions · Identification of applicable protocols · Description of system communication paths · Bandwidth and capacity analysis · Detailed definition of data and resource flows.

Scope – Shall: the resource interactions between physical active resources; the standards and protocols they conform to; the protocols the resources implement. May: traces to logical interactions; the physical passive resources the interactions convey.

Modelling rules – A resource interaction is a flow between two physical active resources of any type, named after what is exchanged, carrying the properties `Protocol` and `Standard` (repeatable); conveyed resources are associated with the flow. A resource implementing a protocol carries the `Protocol` property; a Communication Network is associated with the devices it connects. The Resource Interaction element (Technology Interaction) is used only for the collective behaviour of technology resources. Traceability to L3: the flow links the physical resources that specialise or are associated with the logical resources linked in L3 (P1).

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Protocol and Standard: properties instead of artifacts and contracts; resource interaction: flow by default (the guide's first option), the Resource Interaction element being kept for technology resources.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / P Physical Resource Specifications / P3 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the interactions between physical active resources, the protocols and standards they conform to, and the passive resources they convey.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="P3"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="P – Physical Resource Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="3 – Connectivity"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Technology"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (P3); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 35"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="P4 Resource Functions" id="id-2ed614a4923c4f64a8b8a7ee46283aac">
