            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-3d7e4678286042468671ebc19dbe28bf" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="800" y="20" width="460" height="527"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify the resource functions carried out by resources and the resource flows between them.

Concerns – Capability-based acquisition · Business process and workflow modelling · Human-machine interaction specification · Identification of functional system requirements · Functional decomposition of systems and relation of human and system functions.

Scope – Shall: the physical active resources performing resource functions; the physical passive resources the functions use or deliver; the functional flows and resource flows between functions. May: the passive resources conveyed by resource flows; traces of resource functions to logical behaviour or service functions.

Modelling rules – Each resource is assigned to the Resource Function of its own layer (P1). Functional flow is triggering; a Resource Flow is a specialised flow between resource functions, with conveyed resources associated with it. A logical or service function aggregates the resource functions that implement it. The serving of resources by their functions is allowed and not drawn.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Resource Function: functions instead of processes (P1); Resource Flow: specialised flow instead of a technology interaction.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / P Physical Resource Specifications / P4 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the resource functions carried out by physical resources, the functional and resource flows between them, and the passive resources they use or deliver.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="P4"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="P – Physical Resource Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="4 – Processes"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Layered"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (P4); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 36"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="L4-P4 Activity to Function Mapping" id="id-6a6a4ba371dd43599e6bb64e4a932385">
