            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-22212123491e449389b8ba5d9d864f49" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="616" y="20" width="460" height="459"/>
              <content>Purpose – Link the resource functions to the operational activities of L4 and to the service functions of S4.

Concerns – Requirements definition · Process mapping · Tracing functional system requirements to user requirements · Tracing solution options to requirements · Identification of overlaps.

Scope – Shall: the traceability between resource functions and operational activities. May: traces of resource functions to service functions; the physical active resources performing the resource functions.

Modelling rules – A resource function serves the operational activities it supports; a service function aggregates the resource functions that implement it (as P1, P4). A matrix or table may be produced from these relations by a jArchi report.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Resource Function: functions instead of processes (P1). NAF Steps: L4-P4 is not named in the stage tables of NAF v4.1 ch. 2; AD and AE are those of L4 and P4.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / P Physical Resource Specifications / L4-P4 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Traces resource functions to the operational activities they support and to the service functions they implement.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="L4-P4"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="P – Physical Resource Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="4 – Processes"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Layered"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (L4-P4); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 37"/>
          </element>
