            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-ffe61922ef2449b381b415c11debc921" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="625" y="20" width="460" height="510"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify how resources change state in response to events and other stimuli.

Concerns – Systems engineering · Safety cases · Definition of states, events and state transitions (behavioural modelling).

Scope – Shall: all states of the physical active resources relevant to the entity of interest; the transitions between them. May: the resource events triggering the transitions; the modes of resource functions; traces to logical states.

Modelling rules – Convention of decision S11 (specification-structure.md § 4 bis): `State`, `Initial State` and `State Transition` are properties of the physical active resource; `Mode` is a property of the resource function; the event named in a transition is a Resource Event associated with the resource. A physical resource reuses the state names of the logical resource it specialises or is associated with (P1) to trace them to L5. Label: `${name}` then `States: ${properties:, :State}`.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Resource State, Resource Transition and Resource Mode: properties (decision S11); Resource State Group and functions enabled by a state: not represented; event to resource: association.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / P Physical Resource Specifications / P5 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the possible states of physical active resources, the transitions between them, the events triggering them and the modes of resource functions.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="P5"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="P – Physical Resource Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="5 – States"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="—"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (P5); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 38"/>
          </element>
