            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-80c4cea2a224475a9efc4a41f2361bbf" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="800" y="20" width="460" height="476"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify the data products, data entities and their relationships.

Concerns – System design · Data schema design · Message and protocol specification · Data architecture · Database design · Specifying the data elements exchanged between systems · Security modelling.

Scope – Shall: the data entities relevant to the entity of interest. May: the data model specifying them; their attributes, attribute types and physical characteristics; groupings of entities; traces of data models to information models.

Modelling rules – Entities, models and products are Data Objects, distinguished by their name and documentation. Attributes are properties of the entity, as in L7: key `Attribute` repeated, value `&lt;name>: &lt;type>`; physical characteristics use the key `Physical Characteristic`, value `&lt;name>: &lt;value>`. A data model realises the information model it implements. Detailed schemas belong to a dedicated data modelling tool.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Data Attribute, Data Attribute Type and Physical Characteristic: properties instead of data objects.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / P Physical Resource Specifications / P7 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the data entities, the data models specifying them, the data products, and their relationships.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="P7"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="P – Physical Resource Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="7 – Information"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Information Structure"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (P7); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 40"/>
          </element>
