            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-c164160f12504f67bd0a66f96c5b33fb" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="1167" y="20" width="460" height="476"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify and describe the resource constraints and resource requirements.

Concerns – Non-functional requirements · Safety cases · Definition of implementation logic · Identification of resource constraints.

Scope – Shall: the resource requirements and the resource constraints they relate to; the physical active resources, physical behaviour and physical passive resources they apply to. May: the resource specifications grouping them; the rationale of the constraints, traced to logical constraints.

Modelling rules – As L8: requirements and constraints are realised by the elements they apply to; a resource specification is a Requirement aggregating requirements and constraints; a Rationale (Driver) influences the constraint it justifies and is influenced by the logical constraint it derives from.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Resource Constraint: Constraint instead of a specialised Requirement; physical behaviour: Resource Functions instead of processes (P1); Resource Specification: Requirement without specialisation (decision S2).

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / P Physical Resource Specifications / P8 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies the resource requirements and constraints, and the physical resources and behaviour they apply to.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="P8"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="P – Physical Resource Specifications"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="8 – Constraints"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AD, AE, MP"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Requirements Realization"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (P8); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 41"/>
          </element>
