            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-c15a2436ac584c7d959fb3804415e892" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="816" y="20" width="460" height="425"/>
              <content>Purpose – Record how elements of architecture descriptions correspond to each other, and which methods govern these correspondences.

Concerns – Traceability and dependencies between architectures · Reuse of architectures.

Scope – Shall: the relevant architecture description elements, their correspondences and the correspondence methods. May: how architecture descriptions relate to these elements and correspondences.

Modelling rules – An Element Correspondence is an Association relationship specialised « Element Correspondence » between two Architecture Description Elements (Business Object). A Correspondence Method (Business Process) is associated with that relationship. Name the relationship only when the kind of correspondence adds value.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Element Correspondence: relationship instead of a Representation element.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / A Architecture Meta-Data / A3 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Records the correspondences between elements of architecture descriptions and the methods that govern them.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="A3"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="A – Architecture Meta-Data"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="3 – Connectivity"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AL, AV, AG"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="—"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (A3); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 45"/>
          </element>
