            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-c48926826d774affad67597e42b2e863" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="800" y="20" width="460" height="391"/>
              <content>Purpose – Show which methodologies, and which extensions of them, the architecture projects use.

Concerns – Architecture management and review · Management of architecture projects.

Scope – Shall: the architecture projects, the methodologies they use and the methodology extensions. May: the standards applying to a methodology; the architecture descriptions documenting the projects.

Modelling rules – An Architecture Methodology (Business Process) is associated with the Architecture Project (Work Package) that uses it; an extension specialises its base methodology. Standards applying to a methodology are recorded in its `Standard` property.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Standard: property instead of a Contract element.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / A Architecture Meta-Data / A4 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Shows the architecture projects and the methodologies, and their extensions, that they use.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="A4"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="A – Architecture Meta-Data"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="4 – Processes"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AL, AG"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Project"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (A4); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 46"/>
          </element>
