            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-452ed003bbcb4a26a742026bcd33359a" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="800" y="20" width="460" height="374"/>
              <content>Purpose – Give access to the version history of the architecture work products.

Concerns – Architecture management · Configuration control of architectures.

Scope – Shall: the versions of the work products and their succession. May: the baselines.

Modelling rules – Versions and their succession are Git commits and tags of the Landscape repository; a baseline is a tag of main (decisions A5 and S10). The view lists the Architecture Work Products; each tag is referenced in the CHANGELOG and the governance log, not in the model.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Architecture Version and Architecture Baseline: kept in Git instead of Plateau elements.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / A Architecture Meta-Data / A6 &lt;Subject> (optional).</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Points to the version history of the architecture work products, which is kept in Git.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="A6"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="A – Architecture Meta-Data"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="6 – Sequences"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AL, AG, AC"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="—"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (A6); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 48"/>
          </element>
